content.text:
The final review found real gaps. Three more measured raise paths still give a strict prefix through the interceptor:

- an array in an unknown key, for openai-python;
- a legacy `function_call` extra key that changes type in a middle fragment, for LangChain. This also corrects the P-d row of the spec;
- a choice without `delta` in the record that opens a call.

The review also found the two open must-fix items and a body regression.

These new rules follow D3 of the approved spec (each measured shape becomes a deviation), so I rule on them and run the single fix wave. I write the complete findings list to a file for one fix subagent on Opus.

